<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Trans Caledon Sept 2010 bonds yield 15.3727 pct.</title>
<headline>Trans Caledon Sept 2010 bonds yield 15.3727 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans Caledon Tunnel Authority, a partner in the binational Lesotho Highlands Water Project, said the results of its Wednesday bond tender were as follows:</p>
<p>    Series    Amnt(Rmln)   Av Yield    Range    Previous</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    WS03	85.0	   15.3727    15.38-36  16.2968</p>
<p>    WS02	  -		-	     -	15.9096</p>
<p>    WS01	25.0	   15.21	 15.21	-</p>
<p>(Note - previous results from initial 600 million rand issue made in late Nov 1996.)</p>
<p>The bonds are government guaranteed, in one million rand denominations and settle on the second Thursday after issue.</p>
<p>Funds raised will be applied to the first and second stages of phase one of the project worth 9.8 billion rand and 6.00 billion rand respectively.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
